---
import BaseLayout from "@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout>
  <section>
    <div class="px-8 py-12 mx-auto md:px-12 lg:px-32 max-w-7xl lg:pb-24">
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p>video coming soon...</p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p>
          The OnTrack Education Framework is a research-informed approach to evidence-centred education. It replaces disconnected, high-stakes assessment with clear learning goals, authentic tasks, iterative feedback, and trusted evidence of achievement.

          Students can see where they are, understand what to do next, and improve through feedback. Educators can see learning as it happens and provide timely, targeted support. even across large cohorts.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p>
          OnTrack is better for educators:
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
            <li>See learning as it happens: At-a-glance progress information helps educators identify misconceptions, disengagement, and requests for help before students fall behind.</li>
            <li>Build trusted evidence of capability: Authentic tasks and reflective portfolios capture not only what students produce, but how their knowledge and capabilities develop.</li>
            <li>Make feedback manageable: No more crunch. Instead, support your students with small, frequent, high value formative touch-points.</li>
            <li>Focus support where it matters: Clear task states and learning evidence help teaching teams respond to individual needs while maintaining a view of the whole cohort.</li>
            <li>Maintain meaningful standards: Explicit competency requirements and observable evidence give educators greater confidence that students have demonstrated the intended learning.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p>
          OnTrack is better for students:
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
            <li>Know what success looks like: Clear learning outcomes, transparent standards, and visible pathways help students understand what is expected and how to progress.</li>
            <li>Learn through feedback: Students receive meaningful feedback while they are still learning, with opportunities to respond, improve, and demonstrate mastery.</li>
            <li>Take ownership of learning: Visible progress, flexible goals, and clear next steps give students greater agency while keeping them connected to their teaching team.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto">
        <p>
          OnTrack is better for institutions:
          <ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 list-disc list-outside pl-6">
            <li>Offer a distinctively supportive student experience: Human-centred, evidence-centred education provides a compelling alternative to impersonal, high-stakes assessment.</li>
            <li>Deliver consistent quality at scale: The OnTrack educational framework works with any unit, of any size. You just have to be willing to think a little differently.</li>
            <li>Create learning, don't just measure it: OnTrack makes every task, feedback conversation, and improvement part of a visible learning journey. The result is education that supports student growth, strengthens confidence in graduate capability, and remains meaningful in an AI-pervasive world.</li>
            <li>Support earlier intervention: Visible engagement and progress make it easier to identify students who need support and act while there is still time to help.</li>
          </ul>
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>